      "why": "Full pipelining gives 1 result/cycle, so at Fmax it can clear the 32 results/us throughput and the 0.5us p99-batch bound (32 back-to-back results take 32 cycles; at >=64 MHz that is <=0.5us). It is the cleanest way to meet the system timing bound, but it registers every stage so it is area-heavy; the search should find the smallest (W, N) that still meets max_abs_err <= 2^-12 and see how area scales with N and the guard bits. W=14..16 and N=12..16 bracket the accuracy requirement (accuracy depends only on W, N, guards, rounding), with rounding and small guards to trim area."
